Oh, while I'm here, I have a suggestion of my own:

Wand/spell of time hop. The struck object/monster/player disappears
from time for 1 (or more) turns and then reappears exactly where it was
after it elapses, no time having passed to it. Should it appear
into/onto something else that has moved onto the tile either the thing
is shunted out of the way or simply pushed into by the object and
severely hurt/destroyed depending apon what it is (or perhaps it could
count as devouring should it be a monster and something it can
digest?). Yeah, inspired by the D&D spell which I thought was cool.



